    "section_title": "Section 1. Regulatory Authority & Scope",
    "chunk_index": 1,
    "content": "Regulation SR-402 establishes mandatory cybersecurity controls for all enterprise systems, data\nrepositories, remote workstations, and employee processes (including Process X operations and\nRemote Workflows).",
    "char_count": 208,
    "token_count": 24,
    "metadata": {
      "doc_name": "Enterprise_Security_Regulation_SR402.pdf",
      "page_number": 1,
      "section_title": "Section 1. Regulatory Authority & Scope",
      "version": "1.0",
      "year": "2026",
      "department": "Enterprise Operations",
      "category": "Document",
      "file_path": "nexusrag\\data\\documents\\Enterprise_Security_Regulation_SR402.pdf",
      "checksum": ""
    }
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "Enterprise_Security_Regulation_SR402_pdf_p1_c2",
    "doc_id": "Enterprise_Security_Regulation_SR402_pdf",
    "doc_name": "Enterprise_Security_Regulation_SR402.pdf",
    "doc_type": "pdf",
    "version": "1.0",
    "year": "2026",
    "department": "Enterprise Operations",
    "category": "Document",
    "page_number": 1,
    "section_title": "Section 2. Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA) &",
    "chunk_index": 2,
    "content": "Encryption\nRequirement SEC-01: Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA) is strictly mandatory for all remote access and\nadministrative tools. Hardware security keys or authenticator apps are required. SMS-based 2FA is\nprohibited. Requirement SEC-02: AES-256 encryption is mandated for all data at rest and TLS 1.3 for\ndata in transit.",
    "char_count": 327,
    "token_count": 46,
    "metadata": {
      "doc_name": "Enterprise_Security_Regulation_SR402.pdf",
      "page_number": 1,
      "section_title": "Section 2. Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA) &",
      "version": "1.0",
      "year": "2026",
      "department": "Enterprise Operations",
      "category": "Document",
      "file_path": "nexusrag\\data\\documents\\Enterprise_Security_Regulation_SR402.pdf",
      "checksum": ""
    }
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "Enterprise_Security_Regulation_SR402_pdf_p1_c3",
    "doc_id": "Enterprise_Security_Regulation_SR402_pdf",
    "doc_name": "Enterprise_Security_Regulation_SR402.pdf",
    "doc_type": "pdf",
    "version": "1.0",
    "year": "2026",
    "department": "Enterprise Operations",
    "category": "Document",
    "page_number": 1,
    "section_title": "Section 3. Session Timeout & Inactivity Thresholds",
    "chunk_index": 3,
    "content": "All remote workstation sessions and internal web application logins must automatically lock after 15\nminutes of user inactivity. Screen lock passwords must satisfy the 14-character complexity matrix.",
    "char_count": 199,
    "token_count": 27,
    "metadata": {
